[0;37m  You are about to make an account. This is the whole deal, and
[0;37m  it is shorter than the thing you clicked through this morning.

[1;36m  1.  NO HATE.
[0;32m      ù [0;37mArgue with anybody about anything. Come after a person
[0;32m      ù [0;37mfor who they are and you are off the board. No warning,
[0;32m      ù [0;37mno appeal, no long conversation about it.

[1;36m  2.  NOTHING HERE IS ENCRYPTED.
[0;32m      ù [0;37mThis is telnet, the way it was in 1969. Every word you
[0;32m      ù [0;37mtype crosses the network in the clear, your password
[0;32m      ù [0;37mincluded. Anyone sharing a wire or an access point with
[0;32m      ù [0;37myou can read the lot.

[1;36m  3.  USE A PASSWORD YOU USE NOWHERE ELSE.
[0;32m      ù [0;37mThis is the one that matters. If what you type here is
[0;32m      ù [0;37malso the password on your mail, you have just handed
[0;32m      ù [0;37myour mail to everyone between you and this board. Make
[0;32m      ù [0;37mone up. It does not have to be clever. It has to be new.
